
Adding product image upload functionality to a fully client-side single HTML file ecommerce site means we can allow the user to select an image file from their device, preview it, and add the product with that uploaded image (using a client-side object URL). Since there's no backend, the image won't persist beyond the session, but we can keep it in memory for this session.

Plan:
- Add a section or button to "Add New Product" with fields: product name, price, and image upload input.
- When image is uploaded, preview the image.
- When user submits the form, add the new product to the products array and re-render product grid.
- The image will be stored as a temporary local URL using URL.createObjectURL from the uploaded file.
- Keep all existing functionality (cart, adding to cart) unchanged.
- Add UI for the product upload form somewhere visible, maybe above products grid or as a collapsible section.

No backend, so this is fully client-side and volatile.

Proceed to update the existing single HTML file accordingly.


